okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Unattended restart: start from the last settings without the menu, pass every startup question, send '계속-세션재시작됨' after the session loads (also when there is no conversation to continue), Codex 'Resume paused goal?' -> Leave paused. For restart_session and for a reboot batch script."
requested:
  - "User, 2026-10-12: '마지막에 사용하던 설정을 이용해서 시작 메뉴를 건너뛰고, 자동으로 재시작하게 해주는 또 재시작시 물어보는 기타 질문들을 패스하고 세션로드후. \"계속-세션재시작됨\" 이라는메시지 강제주입. 또 코덱스의 경우 goal이있엇던경우 \"leave goal\" 옵션을 자동으로해주는'."
  - "When: 'restart_session으로 재시작할 때', '시스템문제로 컴퓨터가 재부팅이 되었을때, 배치 스크립트로 사용하기위해서 필요한기능'."
  - "'자동수락해줘야해.. 왜냐면 이것은 24/7 동작하는 머신에 모듈로 동작하는데.. 재시작때 이러한문제때문에 장애 처리가 자동으로 안되고이썽' (trust / bypass dialogs answered too)."
  - "'이어갈 대화가 없어도 계속-세션재시작됨 을넣어야햠.. 그래서 정말 처리내용이 없는지 재확인'."
changes:
  resume_last_flag: "cli_dispatch: --ca-resume-last = --ca-runtime last (launch-state.json by_cwd), no prelaunch menu, no Claude/Codex/Ciel update checks, CIEL_RUNTIME_RESUME_LAST=1 and CIEL_RUNTIME_STARTUP_AUTO_ANSWER=1 for the launcher and its children. session_resume_last.resume_last_passthrough adds --continue: Claude only when ~/.claude (or CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR)/projects/<folder key>/*.jsonl exists ('claude --continue' without one prints 'No conversation found to continue' - string in Claude Code 2.1.296); Codex/codex-remote always, and a missing saved thread now opens a new conversation instead of exiting (runtime_launch Codex TUI: codex_without_resume_command; codex_app_server_resume.resolve_resume_thread returns '' when resume-last)."
  continue_message: "runtime_session_restart.restart_notice_body: message is exactly '계속-세션재시작됨' (RESTART_CONTINUE_MESSAGE), meta raw_injection=true and input_transport=tty, so it is typed into the prompt as is (Claude Code's session socket would present it as 'Another Claude session sent a message', plain Codex's router path as '[ciel-wake] pending_ids=N'). restart_session relaunches and --ca-resume-last launches queue it (Claude, Codex TUI, codex-remote/app-server)."
  cursor_prime: "runtime_session_restart.primed_notice: the channel cursor is initialised before the notice is queued (ciel_runtime.py restart ports). A workspace without channel-llm-cursor.json sets its cursor to the queue tail on first read, which skipped a notice queued just before (codex-remote E2E run 1 phase A)."
  startup_answers: "startup_prompt_answers.StartupPromptResponder, on only for unattended launches (restart_session relaunch sets CIEL_RUNTIME_STARTUP_AUTO_ANSWER=1; --ca-resume-last). Reads the child's screen output (ConPTY output_since on Windows, the pty stream on POSIX), finds a dialog title, then the option: '<n>.<label>' -> that digit (Codex), otherwise the drawn option order and the '❯' marker -> arrow keys + Enter (Claude Code draws no numbers). Waits 0.5 s of quiet output before a key (Claude drops keys within 150 ms of a dialog), retries a redrawn dialog up to 3 times, stops reading output 180 s after start. Channel input waits until no dialog is open (ready footer seen, or 3 s quiet after the last answer)."
  dialogs: "Codex: 'Resume paused goal?' -> Leave paused; 'Trust this folder?' -> Trust and continue (+Enter); 'Update available' -> Skip; resume directory -> Use session directory; model migration -> Use existing model; hooks review -> Trust all and continue; Windows 'Set up the Codex agent sandbox' -> Use non-admin sandbox (+Enter; the admin choice needs a UAC prompt, 3 quits). Claude Code: 'Accessing workspace:' -> Yes, I trust this folder; Bypass Permissions mode -> Yes, I accept; resume from summary -> Resume full session as-is; project .mcp.json server -> Use this MCP server; external CLAUDE.md imports -> Yes, allow; custom API key -> Yes. Texts checked in codex.exe 0.158/0.161 and Claude Code 2.1.296 binaries (strs.py, ctx.py in the session scratchpad); 'Leave paused' was seen on screen (codex 0.162)."
  menu: "Main menu row '20. Unattended restart [script resume-last.cmd | no script]' -> panel: the command for this folder, 'Write restart script' writes <workspace state dir>/resume-last.cmd ('cd /d \"<folder>\"' + 'call ciel-runtime --ca-resume-last'; .sh on POSIX). Registering it to run at boot is left to the operator."
  usage: "cli_usage: --ca-resume-last line."
verification:
  tests: "tests/test_unattended_restart.py (24: responder digits/arrows/Enter/redraw/give-up/ready, sandbox, resume-last passthrough, Claude conversation check, codex resume removal, app-server fallback, primed notice, continue message transport, menu, cli dispatch). Groups: unit OK (skipped 49), router 1189 OK, runtime 405 OK, channel 457 OK on 2 reruns (first run: 2 failures in BoundaryScanDeadlineTests, the known flaky pair that also fails on unmodified HEAD); 3 menu-position tests updated for the new row; ruff clean; router 9611 200."
  e2e_harness: "evidence/e2e_unattended.py (+ e2e_unattended_console.py: passive console watcher, never presses a key; console_driver.py, shot_title.ps1). Isolated config/CODEX_HOME on G:, stub vllm upstream, new Windows Terminal windows running 'python ciel_runtime.py cli --ca-resume-last'. 'Reboot' = every process of the run killed."
  e2e_codex: "evidence/e2e-codex (final run 07:24-07:26): A launch-state codex-remote, no thread -> new thread 01a13012, stub request 1 = '계속-세션재시작됨'; paused goal set over the app-server. B restart_session -> 'startup_prompt_answered prompt=codex_paused_goal option=leavepaused key=2', stub '계속-세션재시작됨', same thread, goal status paused. C reboot, launch-state codex (plain TUI) -> trust (key=1 + Enter), paused goal (Leave paused), Windows sandbox (non-admin + Enter) answered, stub '계속-세션재시작됨' with turn 1 in the history (shots/03: typed '계속-세션재시작됨', 'Sandbox ready', 'Goal paused'). D reboot, codex-remote -> goal answered, '계속-세션재시작됨', same thread, 4 continue messages in the history, goal paused."
  e2e_claude: "evidence/e2e-claude (final run 07:22-07:24): A no conversation -> new one, the prompt typed '계속-세션재시작됨' (stub user message ends with it after Claude Code's <system-reminder> blocks). B restart_session -> again, turn 1 in the history. C reboot -> --continue, '계속-세션재시작됨', turn 1 in the history (shots/03 shows the three typed messages). The folder trust dialog did not appear in the final run (already trusted by run 2); its answer is from run 2: 'startup_prompt_answered prompt=claude_trust option=yes,itrustthisfolder key=downx1+enter', then the session started and took turns (e2e-claude-run2)."
  e2e_menu: "evidence/e2e-menu (menu_e2e.py + menu_drive.py, isolated config): row 20 selected, panel opened, 'Write restart script' -> 'Restart script written: G:\\ciel-e2e\\unattended\\menu\\cfg\\resume-last.cmd' (screen-03-written.png); file text 'cd /d \"G:\\ciel-e2e\\unattended\\menu\\ws\"' / 'call ciel-runtime --ca-resume-last'."
  failures_fixed_on_the_way:
    - "codex run 1 phase A: notice id 1 never injected - first cursor read skips the queue tail -> primed_notice."
    - "codex run 1 phase C: Windows sandbox setup dialog after the trust answer took the typed input ('channel_input_submit_failed reason=prompt_render_timeout') -> codex_windows_sandbox rule."
    - "claude run 1: 'startup_prompt_option_not_found prompt=claude_trust' - Claude draws options without numbers -> arrow-key selection."
    - "claude run 2: session socket delivered the message as 'Another Claude session sent a message: ...' -> input_transport tty."
    - "claude run 3 (aborted): a leftover E2E transcript in ~/.claude/projects/G--ciel-e2e-unattended-claude-ws reused message id 1 ('waiting_for_turn_completion state=queued'); E2E artifact (ids restart with the scratch config), folder removed."
privacy: "stub-requests.json / stub.jsonl of the Claude runs held the user's ~/.claude CLAUDE.md text (Claude Code sends it); deleted from the evidence before commit."
not_verified:
  - "Claude bypass-permissions, resume-from-summary, .mcp.json, external-import and API-key dialogs, and Codex update / model-migration / hooks / resume-directory dialogs: rules unit-tested on screen text from the binaries; not raised in an E2E."
  - "POSIX pty path: unit-level only."
  - "A real reboot of this PC and a live session (no live restart without approval)."
  - "Codex console-input fallback transport (no ConPTY) cannot read the screen: the responder is off there (logged startup_prompt_auto_answer_unavailable)."
observation: "Run 2 of codex: plain Codex TUI receives channel input as '[ciel-wake] pending_ids=N' unless tty transport is used; the continue message now uses tty."
